<title>UK: Vickers says Rolls, Bentley sales rise.</title>
<headline>Vickers says Rolls, Bentley sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vickers Plc said on Monday sales of luxury Rolls-Royce and Bentley cars rose to 1,278 to the end of the third quarter of 1996 compared with 1,082 a year ago.</p>
<p>In a statement, the company said the UK saw sales up 34 percent, the U.S. showed a rise of 18 percent while the Middle East and Africa boosted sales 26 percent.  </p>
<p>Vickers said sales in Japan were two percent up but sales in continental Europe fell 12 percent despite a strong performance from Germany.</p>
<p>Sales in other overseas markets were up 11 percent.</p>
<p>The following table gives a breakdown of the figures:</p>
<p> Area			 To Sept 30 1995	 To Sept 30 1996</p>
<p> UK			   413			 555</p>
<p> Americas		   248			 292</p>
<p> Japan			 83			  85</p>
<p> Middle East &amp; Africa    46			  58</p>
<p> Continental Europe     155			 136</p>
<p> Other overseas	   137			 152</p>
<p> Total			1,082		     1,278</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
